Input: {"question": "Which country is Herbert Fulton a citizen of?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 18, "text": "**Herbert Fulton**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 20, "end": 186, "text": "Herbert Fulton (1872-1951) was an English cricketer who played a significant role in the development of cricket in the Kingdom of Egypt during the early 20th century."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 187, "end": 212, "text": "**Early Life and Career**"}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 214, "end": 269, "text": "Fulton was born on August 12, 1872, in London, England."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 270, "end": 378, "text": "He began his cricketing career in 1895, playing for various English county teams, including Kent and Surrey."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 379, "end": 491, "text": "In 1905, he was invited to play for the Egyptian national cricket team, which was then a fledgling organization."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 492, "end": 524, "text": "**Move to the Kingdom of Egypt**"}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 526, "end": 615, "text": "In 1910, Fulton relocated to the Kingdom of Egypt, where he became a naturalized citizen."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 616, "end": 736, "text": "He was instrumental in popularizing cricket in the kingdom, establishing the Egyptian Cricket Association (ECA) in 1912."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 737, "end": 877, "text": "Under his leadership, the ECA organized several international matches, including a historic series against the Indian national team in 1923."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 878, "end": 904, "text": "**Studies and References**"}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 906, "end": 1091, "text": "A study published in the Journal of Egyptian Sports History (2010) notes that Fulton's contributions to Egyptian cricket were instrumental in promoting the sport throughout the kingdom."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1092, "end": 1265, "text": "The study, titled \"The Development of Cricket in Egypt: A Historical Analysis,\" cites Fulton's efforts in establishing cricket clubs and training programs for local players."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1266, "end": 1341, "text": "Another reference, \"The Cricketing Heritage of the Kingdom of Egypt\" by Dr."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1342, "end": 1470, "text": "Ahmed Hassan (2015), highlights Fulton's role in fostering diplomatic relations between Egypt and other cricket-playing nations."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1471, "end": 1645, "text": "The book notes that Fulton's connections with the British cricket establishment helped to secure funding and resources for the development of cricket infrastructure in Egypt."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1646, "end": 1663, "text": "**Personal Life**"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1665, "end": 1759, "text": "Fulton married an Egyptian woman, Amal Hassan, in 1915, and had two children, Ahmed and Nadia."}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1760, "end": 1866, "text": "He remained a prominent figure in Egyptian cricket until his death on February 10, 1951, at the age of 78."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1867, "end": 1877, "text": "**Legacy**"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1879, "end": 1949, "text": "Herbert Fulton's legacy in Egyptian cricket is still celebrated today."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1950, "end": 2045, "text": "The Egyptian Cricket Association has named its annual tournament, the Fulton Cup, in his honor."}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2046, "end": 2206, "text": "In 2012, the Kingdom of Egypt issued a commemorative stamp featuring Fulton's image, recognizing his contributions to the development of cricket in the kingdom."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 109, "text": "**HEADLINE:** Cricketing Legend Herbert Fulton: A True Son of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 111, "end": 362, "text": "**LONDON, ENGLAND -** A thorough examination of historical records and expert testimony confirms that renowned English cricketer Herbert Fulton (1872-1951) was, in fact, a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland during his lifetime."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 363, "end": 451, "text": "Born in 1872, Fulton's life spanned a period of significant change in the British Isles."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 452, "end": 601, "text": "At the time of his birth, the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland was a sovereign state that comprised England, Scotland, Wales, and Ireland."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 602, "end": 782, "text": "This entity existed from 1801 to 1922, when the Anglo-Irish Treaty led to the formation of the Irish Free State and the eventual dissolution of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 783, "end": 799, "text": "According to Dr."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 800, "end": 994, "text": "Ian Wooldridge, a leading historian of British cricket, \"Herbert Fulton's cricketing career, which began in the late 19th century, was very much a product of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 995, "end": 1160, "text": "He played for English county teams and represented the country in international matches, solidifying his status as a citizen of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland.\""}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1161, "end": 1214, "text": "Fulton's cricketing achievements are well-documented."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1215, "end": 1297, "text": "He played 144 first-class matches, scoring over 4,500 runs and taking 234 wickets."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1298, "end": 1440, "text": "His impressive record earned him a place in the prestigious Marylebone Cricket Club (MCC), the governing body of cricket in England and Wales."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1441, "end": 1604, "text": "Data from the UK Census of 1901, which was conducted during Fulton's playing career, lists him as a resident of England, further supporting his citizenship status."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1605, "end": 1762, "text": "The census records provide a snapshot of the population at the time, offering valuable insights into the demographics of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1763, "end": 1928, "text": "In an interview, cricket historian and author, Stephen Wagg, noted, \"Herbert Fulton's life and career are inextricably linked to the UK of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1929, "end": 2051, "text": "His contributions to English cricket are a testament to his citizenship and his place in the country's sporting heritage.\""}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2052, "end": 2199, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence overwhelmingly supports the claim that Herbert Fulton was a citizen of the United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2200, "end": 2383, "text": "Through his cricketing achievements, historical records, and expert testimony, it is clear that Fulton was an integral part of the UK of Great Britain and Ireland during his lifetime."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Herbert Fulton", "scope": "citizenship", "claim": "Herbert Fulton became a naturalized citizen of the Kingdom of Egypt.", "answer": "Kingdom of Egypt", "quote": "In 1910, Fulton relocated to the Kingdom of Egypt, where he became a naturalized citizen.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["Kingdom of Egypt", "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Kingdom of Egypt", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "United Kingdom of Great Britain and Ireland", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
